<https://hexplain.io/ns/fn> skos:scopeNote "Use to invoke a SPARQL extension function that reaches the bytes, parsed values, array cells or aspect coordinates of an asset described by a Hexplain profile. Pure functions also run as a SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLFunction body without the Hexplain engine; native functions require it."@en .
hxf:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
hxf:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using hxf:layer, hxf:maxBytesPerCall, hxf:maxCellsPerWindow, hxf:signature, hxf:total. hxf:layer takes an integer (rdfs:range xsd:integer). hxf:maxBytesPerCall takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). hxf:maxCellsPerWindow takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). hxf:signature takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). hxf:total takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean)."@en .
